              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Nancy Sharpensteen"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I made this for Easter added a bit of garlic and chunked cheese , &amp; everyone loved it",
            "datePublished": "2016-03-31T18:16:21.357Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Molly"
            },
            "reviewBody": "A nice change for pasta salad. I had leftover mini penne pasta and it worked great in this recipe. I made up half the dressing amount and used an orange bell pepper, as that is what I had on hand. I decreased the sugar, just a tad, and the dressing was great. The dressing alone would be great on a tossed salad. Definitely a salad I would make again, as it is something different, and we like different. Served it with a bowl of spicy chili and we enjoyed the mixture of spice and sweet.",
            "datePublished": "2015-02-17T04:46:42.430Z"
          }
